{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"climactic-deistic-bagworm","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOnce 038d retires the eight old env/config spellings, the published docs and generated reference surfaces must stop presenting them as live aliases. The single-leaf plan review also identified generated/tested surfaces that pin the old names: `docs/env-vars.md`, `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py`, `tests/golden/config_surface.json`, and `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py`.\n\n## Approach\n\nAfter the ADR and runtime children land, regenerate or update every published config/env reference so only canonical spellings remain in live guidance. Keep clearly dated historical references only where they are intentional archival records, and make the release/changelog text name each removed spelling and its canonical replacement. Re-run the full token census so any residual old-name occurrence is classified as either a tombstone/error test, the new ADR, or a clearly historical record.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `docs/env-vars.md`, `docs/config.md`, `docs/config-reference.md`, `docs/bash-migration.md`, `docs/concurrency.md`, `docs/api-stability.md`, `docs/release-notes.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py`, `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py`, and `tests/golden/config_surface.json`\n- any generator or helper invoked to regenerate those published surfaces\n\n## Testing\n\nRun the exact generator/regeneration commands for the env-var and config-surface outputs, prove the updated tests pass, and run a complete-population string sweep across the eight retired spellings to confirm only intentional tombstone/history references remain.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Live documentation and examples use only canonical spellings for the eight removed env/config names.\n- [ ] Generated env/config reference surfaces and their tests are regenerated so they no longer present the old names as live aliases.\n- [ ] Release/changelog documentation names every removal and its canonical replacement.\n- [ ] A full string census of the eight removed spellings leaves only intentional tombstones, the new ADR, or clearly historical references.","id":"1a63-056e-98b9-4ab7","parent_id":"038d-f5ff-b371-4ba5","priority":2,"tags":["janitor","config","breaking-change","compatibility"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Publish canonical config removal docs"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788421647151960001,"uuid":"31974b0d-5732-4df1-8794-10a19ab7b550"}